What "content" means here
-------------------------

CC BY-SA 4.0 applies to the mathematical and editorial prose in this
repository, including:

  - the article, principle and problem text bundled in `src/lib/seed.ts`
  - learning-unit metadata and descriptions in `src/lib/learning-units.ts`
  - the concept-laboratory explanatory copy under `src/components/labs/`
  - the prose documentation under `docs/`

Everything else — TypeScript, React components, build scripts, configuration
and test code — is MIT-licensed software, even when it happens to contain a
short descriptive string.

Where a single file mixes both (for example a component whose JSX contains
substantial explanatory prose), the code is MIT and the prose is CC BY-SA 4.0.


